note:
Ивањдан is the Nativity of John the Baptist, on July 7. It is called «the girls' feast».

Customs:
• on the eve a вѐнчић is woven from yellow иванско цвеће and hung on the gate until next year;
• water is said to gain special power on this day, so people swim in rivers and lakes;
• in the past bonfires were lit around villages.

The feast is linked with the summer solstice and the ancient cult of the Sun.
